course: dictionary
lesson: 3478
title: Three meanings of false
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «False» is an adjective, and it has three main meanings. The first is not true or not correct: «3 + 4 = 8» is false, because 3 + 4 is 7. The second is not real, made to look like something else, like false teeth. The third is not honest or not loyal, like a false friend.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. In «A false alarm», the alarm rang but there was no danger, so false means not real. In «a false friend pretends to like you», the clue is pretends, so false means not honest. Ask yourself: is this about a statement, a copy, or a person?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If you think false means not true, put «not true» in place of false. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: False means not true or not correct.
fact: A claim is true or false all by itself, whoever says it.
fact: «Not» flips true and false.
fact: «A false alarm» means an alarm rang when there was no danger, but always leave the building when a fire alarm rings.
fact: «The thorny devil has a false head on its neck that it shows when attacked.» Here false means not real.
exercise: In maths, «3 + 4 = 8» is shown as a sum. Why is it called false? | *It is not correct, because 3 + 4 is 7 | It is not honest | It is a longer sum than the others | It is made to look like a sum
exercise: «A false alarm» rang, but there was no danger. What does false mean? | Not loud enough to hear | Not honest: it tried to trick people | *Not real: it rang when there was no danger
exercise: «False friends pretend to like you.» What does false mean here? | Not tall | Made of paper | *Not honest or not loyal | Not hungry
test: A statement says «Two plus two is five». What is it? | True | Real | Loyal | *False
test: «The thorny devil has a false head on its neck.» What does false mean here? | Not true, with wrong facts | Not honest | Loyal to a friend | *Not real, made to look like something else
exam: «Not» is a tiny word in «Not» flips true and false. What does adding «not» do to a true statement? | It makes it louder | *It turns it into a false statement | It stops it being a sentence | It makes it true twice
